[{:db/id "q-325351/field-1/f2ca1abf3b80880f33d1bd9f439b7db8751b148de0fcb4acc24a1c2eaba81987" :answer/id #uuid "26b69da2-d663-5c1e-9614-b91c4385132d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}(x-5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325351/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8b5ed917-dec8-5b00-a5d2-ede945656720" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-325351/field-1/f2ca1abf3b80880f33d1bd9f439b7db8751b148de0fcb4acc24a1c2eaba81987" :answer-field/choices ["q-325351/field-1/f2ca1abf3b80880f33d1bd9f439b7db8751b148de0fcb4acc24a1c2eaba81987"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-325351" :question/id #uuid "e8c36a82-4021-5469-908b-8de473f8be8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-325351" :question/problem "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1.$\n\n$y=\\pm $\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n(h,k)=(5,0),\\,a=\\sqrt{9}=3,\\,b=\\sqrt{16}=4.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-0 & =\\pm (\\frac{4}{3})(x-5) \\\\ y & =\\pm \\,\\frac{4}{3}(x-5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-325351/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c96e6d6f-22be-5bfd-b24e-be9e34fcb149"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-325351"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-10472/selection/4b4fa6c88d65e105d2dc61ce1fcb87a41e364218385e42556af71494609a9fb7" :answer/id #uuid "ab7b4798-2611-53ef-8ecf-dc51a386f607" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y+2=\\pm \\frac{4}{9}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-10472/selection/91940077b468babf9bbda4b9