}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n(h,k)=(0,-2),\\,a=\\sqrt{25}=5,\\,b=\\sqrt{4}=2.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\ny+2=\\pm \\frac{2}{5}x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-86650/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c96e6d6f-22be-5bfd-b24e-be9e34fcb149"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-86650"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-325348/field-1/e15ed5c59fc4311abfa96603d9dd83cdb2d92e51e0085de7af6fa071246831b5" :answer/id #uuid "3331a03e-7974-58a0-b50c-a033eee11aa8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3(x-7)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-325348/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e3f1f941-0747-59c0-b4db-d88ce9133b49" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-325348/field-1/e15ed5c59fc4311abfa96603d9dd83cdb2d92e51e0085de7af6fa071246831b5" :answer-field/choices ["q-325348/field-1/e15ed5c59fc4311abfa96603d9dd83cdb2d92e51e0085de7af6fa071246831b5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-325348" :question/id #uuid "96fcb93f-cc36-54fe-9086-2e51445cb005" :question/math-academy-id "q-325348" :question/problem "Calculate the asymptotes of the hyperbola $(x-7)^{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1.$\n\n$y=\\pm $\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at ((h,k)) is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny-k=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}(x-h).\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have \n\n$$\n(h,k)=(7,0),\\,a=\\sqrt{1}=1,\\,b=\\sqrt{9}=3.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-0 & =\\pm (\\frac{3}{1})(x-7) \\\\ y & =\\pm \\,3(x-7).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficu